EXT. MANGROVE SWAMP - DUSK

Roots like knuckles. Black water, glassy, ringed with mosquitoes. A heavy sky bruised orange and green. The air tastes of rot and salt.

Four people wade single file, waist-deep. Packs held over their heads.

ELSPETH GRAY, 50s, in a drenched canvas hat, leads. Her face is lined, sunburnt, patient. She tests each step with a bamboo pole.

WANJIRU KARIUKI, 30s, close behind, wears a field vest with too many pockets. Her braid is plastered to her neck. She carries the sat-phone, dead for three days.

HENRIK DAHL, 40s, tall and blond, grey with fever, stumbles through the rear. His glasses are cracked.

YUSUF AL-RASHID, 20s, the youngest, carries Henrik's pack as well as his own. He grins when he thinks no one's watching.

ELSPETH
Roots ahead. Step high.

WANJIRU
How far to the river?

ELSPETH
Two miles. Maybe three.

WANJIRU
Maybe is an expensive word.

ELSPETH
It's the only one I've got.

She plants her pole. Water ripples around her thighs. She stops.

ELSPETH (CONT'D)
Stay still.

They do. A long beat. Frogs fall silent.

Something large breaks the surface twenty feet away. A dark ridge, a pair of eyes. It glides toward the nearest root and slides beneath it.

Nobody breathes.

YUSUF
(whispering)
Is it a log?

ELSPETH
It's not a log.

YUSUF
Is it going to eat us?

WANJIRU
It's been eating the whole way. We're just the dessert.

HENRIK
(hoarse)
Wanji.

WANJIRU
Henrik. Don't talk.

HENRIK
I need to sit.

WANJIRU
You can't sit. It's a swamp.

HENRIK
I'm going to sit anyway.

YUSUF
I've got him.

He braces Henrik. Elspeth glares at the root where the shape vanished. She waves a hand: forward.

They move. Slowly, silently, a procession of damp shadows across the dusk.

ELSPETH
Single file. Keep to the left bank. The right is deeper.

WANJIRU
How do you know?

ELSPETH
I came here thirty years ago. With my husband.

WANJIRU
What happened?

ELSPETH
He went to the right bank.

Nobody asks more.

They wade on. Henrik coughs, a cracked wet sound. Yusuf pats his back. Wanjiru adjusts the sat-phone on her shoulder. She tries the power switch. Nothing.

WANJIRU (CONT'D)
(under her breath)
Come on. Come on.

The sky darkens a shade. Fireflies bloom in the branches overhead, hundreds, drifting down like green sparks.

YUSUF
It's beautiful.

HENRIK
It's malaria.

YUSUF
Can't it be both?

HENRIK
(a faint smile)
Possibly.

ELSPETH
Quiet now. We cross the channel in front of us. Hold hands.

They link: Elspeth, Wanjiru, Yusuf, Henrik. A chain across the black water.

ELSPETH (CONT'D)
On three. One. Two.

Something SPLASHES behind them.

ELSPETH (CONT'D)
Go!

They plunge forward. Water surges to their chests. Yusuf pulls Henrik, who is half-floating. Wanjiru holds the phone high. Elspeth thrashes ahead, bamboo pole cutting a path.

They reach the far bank. Haul themselves up into mud and roots. Collapse, gasping.

Behind them, a long ripple fades across the channel.

WANJIRU
(laughing, crying)
We made it.

ELSPETH
We made the channel.

YUSUF
There's more?

ELSPETH
Two miles.

He lies back. Stares at the sky. Fireflies drift across his face.

YUSUF
Okay.
